/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
|       \|/    C hemicals     |  PEQ 2026-27 -- Green ammonia, industrial N2  |
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  SECTOR RECOVERY -- what happens to the purge.

   Purge (250 K, 200 bar) --[PurgeValve]--[PurgeHeater]--+
                               -> 30 bar     -> ~300 K   |
                                                         v
                             WashWater ------------->[Scrubber]
                                                      |       |
                                            ScrubbedGas       AqueousNH3
                                          (H2, N2, Ar)        (~3 % NH3)

  WHY THIS IS A SECTOR OF ITS OWN.  It cannot live in LOOP: everything here
  runs at 30 bar, and the loop is at 200.  It cannot live in PURIFICATION
  either: that is the front of the plant, this is the back.  And it needs its
  own property package (water as the solvent), which is a sector-level thing.

  WHAT IS NOT HERE YET, and the reason it is not.  A membrane or PSA behind
  the scrubber would send the recovered hydrogen -- about 1.1 M EUR/year --
  back to the synthesis compressor suction, in PURIFICATION.  That closes a
  recycle running LOOP -> RECOVERY -> PURIFICATION -> LOOP, i.e. through ALL
  THREE sectors.  The rule this plant's geography was drawn on is "cut where
  the recycle does not pass", so such a tear belongs to no sector: it would
  have to be declared at the PLANT root, which is a composite node like any
  other and may declare one.
    There is also a data obstacle, and it is worth knowing before you try: the
  `psa` unit needs an adsorption isotherm per species, and the catalogue's
  zeolite5A has H2, N2, CH4, CO2 and CO -- but NOT argon.  A species with no
  isotherm is treated as NON-adsorbing and reports to the raffinate, so the
  argon would ride back into the loop with the recovered hydrogen and the
  purge would stop doing its job entirely.  Authoring an Ar/zeolite5A isotherm
  is the prerequisite.

  The water circuit of a real unit (column bottoms back to the column top) is
  a recycle INTERNAL to this sector, so this sector would own that tear -- one
  more sign the grouping is right.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
sectors    ( PurgeValve  PurgeHeater  Scrubber );

boundary
{
    inlets   ( Purge  WashWater );
    outlets  ( ScrubbedGas  AqueousNH3 );
}

connections
{
    Purge        { to PurgeValve/Feed; }
    PurgeLP      { from PurgeValve/Out;    to PurgeHeater/Feed; }
    PurgeWarm    { from PurgeHeater/Out;   to Scrubber/Gas; }
    WashWater    { to Scrubber/Water; }
    ScrubbedGas  { from Scrubber/CleanGas; }
    AqueousNH3   { from Scrubber/RichLiquid; }
}
